data_Li6PS5Cl_argyrodite_reduced
# REDUCED FIXTURE — NOT a real Li6PS5Cl primitive cell.
# Real argyrodite Li6PS5Cl is space group F-43m (#216), conventional cubic
# cell a ≈ 9.86 Å, 4 formula units (52 atoms in conventional cell).
# We use the real conventional lattice parameter and place ONE formula unit
# (13 atoms: 6Li + 1P + 5S + 1Cl) at illustrative argyrodite Wyckoff
# positions; this is suitable as a stoichiometry/disorder fixture but is
# NOT a relaxed primitive cell. The real cell exhibits S/Cl partial
# occupancy (the disorder that lowers conductivity in some samples) — this
# fixture uses ordered positions; downstream Phase 0 / L1 adapters that
# need the disorder model will load the full SOD-generated supercell.
#
# Argyrodite is the PRD §Scope "known-borderline control": good ionic
# conductivity potential but Li-metal interface and moisture sensitivity
# concerns. The fixture purpose is to drive the L1 + ionic-transport
# pipeline through a structure with known thermochemical complexity and
# to populate the falsifier rows for interface_stability and oxidative
# stability.
#
# Sources:
#   - Deiseroth, H. J. et al. "Li6PS5X: A Class of Crystalline Li-Rich
#     Solids with an Unusually High Li+ Mobility", Angew. Chem. Int. Ed.
#     47(4), 755–758 (2008). DOI: 10.1002/anie.200703900
#   - Boulineau, S. et al. "Mechanochemical synthesis of Li-argyrodite
#     Li6PS5X (X=Cl,Br,I) as sulfur-based solid electrolytes for all
#     solid state lithium batteries application", Solid State Ionics 221,
#     1–5 (2012). DOI: 10.1016/j.ssi.2012.06.008
#   - Materials Project entry mp-985592 (Li6PS5Cl argyrodite).
_cell_length_a 9.859
